48:48.708 --> 48:55.458
Praise God!

48:55.958 --> 48:59.373
So the Holy Spirit prompts us, but you must learn how to

48:59.406 --> 49:00.716
respond to this prompting.

49:03.867 --> 49:07.278
He will pour out the Spirit of grace and supplication.

49:07.504 --> 49:09.622
You must learn how to respond to it.

49:11.643 --> 49:15.182
The reason it looks as if you don't have a prayer life, the reason

49:15.682 --> 49:19.850
it looks as though you don't pray when you ought to, is because you always

49:20.044 --> 49:24.721
rely on your own strength. You always judge that moment

49:25.043 --> 49:27.556
by how you feel. There is supply.

49:29.329 --> 49:36.379
And I'm telling you, the supply of God's Spirit is epichoregia.

49:36.849 --> 49:40.274
Amen. Oh, glory to God. How many of you

49:40.774 --> 49:44.174
still remember that teaching? My daughter was sharing

49:44.207 --> 49:47.748
that message with me on— I mean, yesterday on the dining. I said,

49:47.845 --> 49:50.977
do you remember the message you preached on epichoregia? I was

49:51.477 --> 49:54.854
like, how will you even be— I had to rehearse the Greek word before I

49:54.919 --> 49:57.188
mastered it. And you just say it casually like that.

50:00.850 --> 50:04.175
The supply of the Spirit is not always at the

50:04.675 --> 50:09.622
level of your need. It always surpasses

50:10.122 --> 50:14.162
that. Even if you're at your lowest point, the supply of the Spirit

50:14.662 --> 50:18.061
of grace will be so overwhelming that you will float

50:18.109 --> 50:18.983
out of the valley.

50:24.393 --> 50:27.045
But you must learn to respond to the prompting.

50:29.252 --> 50:32.565
I've said it so many times that that sad

50:33.065 --> 50:36.891
feeling— not every sad emotion is a

50:37.020 --> 50:40.193
depression. Sometimes it is the

50:40.338 --> 50:44.107
